WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.925
DNA wraps around histone proteins.

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:06.382
Tight packing is heterochromatin;
loose packing is euchromatin.

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:09.303
Now add methyl groups at a promoter.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:13.700
The supplied cancer example
links heavy promoter methylation with

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:15.500
reduced tumor-suppressor transcription.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.573
The base sequence need not change.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:20.832
A chemical modification can change gene activity.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:25.135
Different expression patterns help
cells acquire different identities, even

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:26.667
when they carry the same DNA.
